// @error cannot infer a type for parameter `n`
// An arrow-lambda param with NO contextual type is genuinely uninferable when the lambda is NOT a
// value binding and the un-annotated higher-order parameter it is passed to is neither called nor
// dropped by the callee's body: `ident(f)` only hands it back, so no call site types `n`. The
// compiler asks for an annotation rather than letting an `Unknown` reach codegen. (A callee that
// calls the parameter types the lambda from that call — see
// hole-lambda-typed-by-callee-call.vl; a lambda bound to an un-annotated `const`/`let`
// value-flow-monomorphizes per call — see lambda-binding-valueflow.vl.)
function ident(f) { return f }

print(ident((n) => n * 2)(3))
